/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTDetectors StMuDSTMaker — Detector Subsystem Data Classes
 * @brief Per-detector hit, collection, PID traits, and utility classes in the MuDST.
 * @details
 * Every STAR detector subsystem represented in the MuDST follows a four-class pattern:
 *   - **StMu\<Det\>Hit** — stores one calibrated hardware measurement (hardware address
 *     fields such as tray/module/cell, plus physics quantities such as time, charge,
 *     and local position).
 *   - **StMu\<Det\>Collection** — event-level container (TClonesArray or std::vector
 *     wrapper), sometimes augmented with a header or digi sub-array.
 *   - **StMu\<Det\>PidTraits** — quantities resulting from matching a reconstructed
 *     track to a hit: local impact coordinates, measured TOF, path length, β, Nσ,
 *     and PID probabilities.  Stored *inside* StMuTrack, not in a separate branch.
 *   - **StMu\<Det\>Util** — bidirectional converter between StEvent's
 *     St\<Det\>Collection and the MuDST TClonesArrays; called by StMuDSTMaker during
 *     writing and by StMuDst during reading.
 *
 * Branch names used in the MuDST TTree are registered in StMuArrays.
 *
 * @see DETECTORS.md for the full reference including field tables, accessors,
 *      branch names, and PID traits usage examples.
 * @{
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTBTOF Barrel Time-of-Flight (BTOF)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Barrel Time-of-Flight detector.
 * @details
 * The BTOF identifies charged hadrons (π/K/p) via time-of-flight measurement in
 * |η| < 0.9 using 120 trays of Multi-gap Resistive Plate Chambers (MRPCs),
 * each tray containing 32 modules of 6 cells.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuBTofHit — one calibrated MRPC cell hit.  Hardware address: tray [1,120],
 *     module [1,32], cell [1,6].  Physics: leading-edge time (ns), trailing-edge time
 *     (ns), tot() = trailing − leading.  Also stores indices into the primary and
 *     global track arrays (index2Primary, index2Global) and MC truth fields
 *     (idTruth, qaTruth).
 *   - StMuBTofHitCollection — std::vector<StMuBTofHit*> wrapper.
 *   - StMuBTofPidTraits — embedded in StMuTrack::mBTofPidTraits.  Fields:
 *     matchFlag, yLocal/zLocal (cm), thetaLocal (rad), position (StThreeVectorF),
 *     timeOfFlight (ns), pathLength (cm), beta, sigmaElectron/Pion/Kaon/Proton (Nσ),
 *     probElectron/Pion/Kaon/Proton.  Retrieved via StMuTrack::btofPidTraits().
 *   - StMuBTofUtil — converts StBTofCollection ↔ StMuBTofHitCollection via
 *     getMuBTofHit() and fillMuBTofHit().
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** BTofHit, BTofRawHit, BTofHeader
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTETOF Endcap Time-of-Flight (ETOF)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Endcap Time-of-Flight detector.
 * @details
 * The ETOF extends TOF PID into the forward pseudorapidity range 1.6 < η < 2.2
 * using MRPC counters arranged in 3 z-planes × 3 counters × 12 sectors.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuETofDigi — one electronic channel (one MRPC strip side) readout.
 *     Hardware address: rocId, get4Id, elChan (electronics); or sector [7–18],
 *     zPlane [1–3], counter [1–3], strip, side (geometry).  Physics: rawTime,
 *     calibTime, rawTot, calibTot (all in ns).  Links to parent StMuETofHit via
 *     associatedHitId.
 *   - StMuETofHit — one reconstructed MRPC hit from ≥ 2 digis on opposite sides.
 *     Hardware address: sector, zPlane, counter.  Physics: time (ns), totalTot (ns),
 *     clusterSize, localX/localY (cm).  Track links: associatedTrackId,
 *     index2Primary, index2Global.  MC truth: idTruth, qaTruth.
 *   - StMuETofHeader — event-level trigger/timing: trgGdpbFullTime and
 *     trgStarFullTime (ns), per-ROC timestamp maps (rocGdpbTs, rocStarTs),
 *     STAR token/DAQ/TRG command words, eventStatusFlag, per-Get4 mismatch flags
 *     (missMatchFlagVec), and per-counter good-event flags (goodEventFlagVec).
 *   - StMuETofCollection — event-level container holding one StMuETofHeader plus
 *     std::vector containers of StMuETofDigi and StMuETofHit.  Accessors:
 *     etofHeader(), etofDigi(i), etofHit(i), digisPresent(), hitsPresent().
 *   - StMuETofPidTraits — embedded in StMuTrack::mETofPidTraits.  Fields:
 *     matchFlag, localX/localY (cm), deltaX/deltaY (cm, residuals), thetaLocal
 *     (rad), position, timeOfFlight (ns), pathLength (cm), beta.
 *     Retrieved via StMuTrack::etofPidTraits().
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** ETofDigi, ETofHit, ETofHeader
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTLegacyTOF Legacy TOF
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the legacy STAR scintillator TOF system.
 * @details
 * The legacy TOF preceded the BTOF.  These classes are retained for backward
 * compatibility with Run-5 and earlier data.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuTofHit — one scintillator hit with embedded PID.  Hardware address:
 *     trayIndex, moduleIndex, cellIndex, daqIndex.  Raw data: adc.  Physics:
 *     timeOfFlight (ns), pathLength (cm), beta, projectedPoint (StThreeVectorF).
 *     PID: tofExpectedAs{Electron,Pion,Kaon,Proton} (ns), sigma{...} (Nσ),
 *     particleHypothesis.
 *   - StMuTofHitCollection — std::vector<StMuTofHit*> wrapper.
 *   - StMuTofUtil — converts StTofCollection ↔ StMuTofHitCollection via
 *     getMuTofHit() and fillMuTofHit().
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** TofHit, TofData, TofRawData
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTMTD Muon Telescope Detector (MTD)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Muon Telescope Detector.
 * @details
 * The MTD identifies muons using MRPCs mounted on the outer steel of the STAR
 * magnet, covering |η| < 0.5 across 30 backlegs × 5 modules × 12 cells.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuMtdHit — one calibrated MRPC hit.  Hardware address: backleg [1,30],
 *     module [1,5], cell [0,11].  Physics: leadingEdgeTime and trailingEdgeTime
 *     as pair<Double_t,Double_t> (ns, one per readout end), tof().  Track links:
 *     associatedTrackKey, index2Primary, index2Global.  MC: idTruth, qaTruth.
 *   - StMuMtdRawHit — one raw TDC edge before hit reconstruction.  Fields:
 *     flag (leading/trailing), backleg, channel, tdc.
 *   - StMuMtdHeader — event-level trigger header.  Stores two fiber headers,
 *     trigger words, trigger times, shouldHaveRejectEvent (0/1/2), and
 *     tpcSectorMask.
 *   - StMuMtdCollection — wraps StMuMtdHeader, StMuMtdHit, and StMuMtdRawHit
 *     in std::vector containers.  Accessors: mtdHeader(), MtdHit(i), RawMtdHit(i).
 *   - StMuMtdPidTraits — embedded in StMuTrack::mMtdPidTraits.  Fields:
 *     matchFlag, yLocal/zLocal (cm), deltaY/deltaZ (cm, residuals), thetaLocal
 *     (rad), position, timeOfFlight (ns), expTimeOfFlight (ns), pathLength (cm),
 *     beta, sigmaMuon (Nσ), probMuon.  Retrieved via StMuTrack::mtdPidTraits().
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** MTDHit, MTDRawHit, MTDHeader
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTEPD Event Plane Detector (EPD)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Event Plane Detector.
 * @details
 * The EPD measures charged-particle multiplicity in 2.1 < |η| < 5.1 using two
 * scintillator tile wheels (East/West), each with 12 supersectors × 31 tiles.
 * Total object size is 10 bytes per hit.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuEpdHit — one tile signal.  mId (Short_t): sign = ±1 (West/East),
 *     |abs| = 100 × position + tile.  mQTdata (Int_t): packed bits 0–11 = ADC
 *     [0,4095], 12–23 = TAC [0,4095], 24–28 = TDC [0,31], 29 = hasTAC,
 *     30 = isGood (database status).  mnMIP (Float_t): gain-calibrated energy
 *     loss in units of Landau MPV for one MIP.  mTruthId: MC particle id.
 *     Accessors: id(), side(), position() [1,12], tile() [1,31], adc(), tac(),
 *     tdc(), hasTac(), isGood(), nMIP(), idTruth().
 *   - StMuEpdHitCollection — std::vector<StMuEpdHit*> wrapper.
 *   - StMuEpdUtil — converts StEpdCollection ↔ StMuEpdHitCollection via
 *     getMuEpdHit() and fillMuEpdHit().
 *
 * **MuDST branch:** EpdHit
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTEMC Electromagnetic Calorimeters (EMC)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Barrel and Endcap Electromagnetic Calorimeters.
 * @details
 * The BEMC (|η| < 1, 4800 Pb-scintillator towers) and EEMC (1.08 < η < 2.0,
 * 720 towers) each have pre-shower (PRS) and shower-maximum detector (SMD) layers.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuEmcHit — one PRS or SMD strip hit.  Fields: id, adc, calType, energy (GeV).
 *   - StMuEmcTowerData — packed tower ADC arrays.  Stores 4800 BEMC tower ADCs and
 *     720 EEMC tower ADCs (UShort_t each), plus crate status bytes (30 BEMC tower
 *     crates, 8 BEMC SMD crates, etc.).  Accessor: towerADC(id, detector).
 *   - StMuEmcCluster — one shower cluster.  Fields: eta, phi, sigmaEta, sigmaPhi,
 *     energy (GeV), nHits, TArrayS of hit indices.
 *   - StMuEmcPoint — one reconstructed photon/electron position.  Fields: eta, phi,
 *     radius (cm), deltaEta, deltaPhi, energy (GeV), chiSquare.  Holds pointers to
 *     associated clusters for each of the 8 sub-detectors.
 *   - StMuEmcCollection — top-level container.  Provides getTowerADC(id, detector),
 *     getPrsHit/getSmdHit/getCluster/getPoint and EEMC-specific accessors.
 *     Sub-detector codes: bemc=1, bprs=2, bsmde=3, bsmdp=4, eemc=5, eprs=6,
 *     esmdu=7, esmdv=8.
 *   - StMuEmcUtil — converts StEmcCollection ↔ StMuEmcCollection via getMuEmc(),
 *     getEmc(), fillMuEmc(), fillEmc().  Uses StEmcGeom for geometry.
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** EmcTow, EmcPrs, EmcSmde, EmcSmdp
 * (EEMC data is in the same StMuEmcCollection object via EEMC-specific accessors.)
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTFMS Forward Meson Spectrometer (FMS)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Forward Meson Spectrometer.
 * @details
 * The FMS measures photons and neutral mesons (π⁰, η) at forward rapidity
 * 2.6 < η < 4.0 using lead-glass cells read out by QT boards.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuFmsHit — one cell signal.  Fields: detectorId, channel, qtCrate, qtSlot,
 *     qtChannel (packed into mQTCrtSlotCh), adc, tdc, energy (GeV).
 *   - StMuFmsCluster — a contiguous group of towers.  Fields: detectorId, category
 *     (EFmsClusterCategory), energy (GeV), x/y (cm, center-of-gravity), sigmaMin,
 *     sigmaMax (2nd moments), chi2Ndf1Photon, chi2Ndf2Photon, id.  TRefArrays:
 *     mHits (member cells), mPhotons (fitted StMuFmsPoint objects).
 *   - StMuFmsPoint — energy from one photon.  Fields: detectorId, energy (GeV),
 *     x/y (cm, local), id, mXYZ (StThreeVectorF, STAR global), mCluster (TRef).
 *     Methods: momentum(m, zvertex) → StThreeVectorF;
 *     fourMomentum(m, zvertex) → StLorentzVectorF.
 *   - StMuFmsCollection — holds TClonesArrays for hits, clusters, points, and one
 *     StMuFmsInfo entry.  Also stores fmsReconstructionFlag.
 *   - StMuFmsUtil — converts StFmsCollection ↔ StMuFmsCollection.  Static method
 *     fillMuFmsHits(StMuFmsCollection&, StTriggerData&) allows recovery of FMS hits
 *     from the trigger data block.
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** FmsHit, FmsCluster, FmsPoint, FmsInfo
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTFCS Forward Calorimeter System (FCS)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Forward Calorimeter System.
 * @details
 * The FCS consists of an ECAL arm (W-Pb Shashlik, 4.0 < η < 5.1) and an HCAL arm
 * (Pb-scintillator, 2.3 < η < 4.5).  Replaces and extends the FMS for BES-II era.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuFcsHit — one calorimeter cell with full timebin waveform.  mDetId
 *     (UShort_t): bit 15 = ZS flag, bits 12–14 = detector id, bits 0–11 = cell id.
 *     mDepCh (UShort_t): packed NS/EHP/DEP/channel.  mAdcSum, mFitPeak, mFitSigma,
 *     mFitChi2, mNPeak, mEnergy (GeV).  mData (TArrayS): 16-bit packed ADC+flag per
 *     timebin.  mCluster (TRef): parent cluster.
 *   - StMuFcsCluster — shower cluster.  Fields: id, detectorId, category, nTowers,
 *     energy (GeV), x/y (local grid, 1st moment), sigmaMin/sigmaMax/theta (2nd
 *     moments and orientation), chi2Ndf1Photon, chi2Ndf2Photon, mFourMomentum
 *     (TLorentzVector).  TRefArrays: mHits, mNeighbor, mPoints.
 *   - StMuFcsPoint — one fitted particle in a cluster.  Fields: detectorId, energy
 *     (GeV), x/y (local cell units), nParentClusterPhotons, mXYZ (TVector3),
 *     mFourMomentum (TLorentzVector), mCluster (TRef).
 *   - StMuFcsInfo — event-level bookkeeping: fcsReconstructionFlag and
 *     per-detector first-hit/cluster/point index arrays (mHitIndex[kFcsNDet+2],
 *     mClusterIndex[kFcsNDet+1], mPointIndex[kFcsNDet+1]) for O(1) per-detector
 *     lookup.
 *   - StMuFcsCollection — holds TClonesArrays for hits, clusters, points, info.
 *     Provides indexOfFirstHit(idet), numberOfHits(idet), etc.
 *   - StMuFcsUtil — converts StFcsCollection ↔ StMuFcsCollection.  Maintains
 *     in-memory maps (mMapHits, mMapClusters, mMapPoints) to rebuild cross-
 *     references during the fill.
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** FcsHit, FcsCluster, FcsPoint, FcsInfo
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTFGT Forward GEM Tracker (FGT)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Forward GEM Tracker.
 * @details
 * The FGT tracks charged particles at 1 < η < 2 using six GEM discs, each divided
 * into four quadrants with two strip planes (r and φ) × 720 strips.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuFgtStrip — one calibrated strip.  Fields: mGeoId (Int_t, encodes
 *     6 disc × 4 quad × 2 plane × 720 strip), mAdcStartIdx (index into the FgtAdc
 *     TClonesArray), mNumSavedTimeBins, mClusterSeedType (StEvent enumeration),
 *     mCharge (Float_t, C; ADC = ped + charge × gain), mChargeUncert.
 *   - StMuFgtAdc — one ADC sample for one strip at one timebin.  Fields: mAdc
 *     (Short_t), mTimeBin (Short_t).  Negative values indicate uninitialised.
 *   - StMuFgtCluster — one 1-D cluster.  Fields: mCentralStripGeoId (cluster key),
 *     mFirstStripAssociationIdx (start of this cluster's entries in the
 *     FgtStripAssociation array), mNumStrips, mMaxTimeBin, mMaxAdc, mCharge,
 *     mChargeUncert, mR/mErrR/mPhi/mErrPhi (position and error), mEvenOddChargeAsy
 *     ((even − odd) / sum charge asymmetry for φ layer).
 *   - StMuFgtStripAssociation — membership record linking one strip to one cluster.
 *     Fields: mClusIdx (cluster index), mStripIdx (strip index), mWeight (membership
 *     weight).
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** FgtStrip, FgtCluster, FgtStripAssociation, FgtAdc
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTPMD Photon Multiplicity Detector (PMD)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Photon Multiplicity Detector.
 * @details
 * The PMD measures photon multiplicity at 2.3 < η < 3.5 using gas-detector cells in
 * two planes: the PMD (photon detector) and the CPV (charged-particle veto).
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuPmdHit — one cell signal.  Fields: superModule (Short_t), subDetector,
 *     row, col, energy (Float_t, MeV), adc (Int_t).
 *   - StMuPmdCluster — one reconstructed cluster.  Fields: superModule, ncell,
 *     eta, phi, sigma (cluster spread), energy (MeV), energyPID (PID from energy
 *     threshold), PID (alternate method, e.g. neural network), mcPID (GEANT truth,
 *     0 for data).
 *   - StMuPmdCollection — holds TClonesArrays for hits and clusters separately for
 *     PMD (pmd=1) and CPV (cpv=2).  Accessors: getCluster(id, detector),
 *     getHit(id, detector), getNClusters(detector), getNHits(detector).
 *   - StMuPmdUtil — converts StPhmdCollection ↔ StMuPmdCollection via getMuPmd(),
 *     getPmd(), fillMuPmd(), fillPmd().
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** PmdHit, CpvHit, PmdCluster, CpvCluster
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTRPS Roman Pot Spectrometer (RPS)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Roman Pot Spectrometer.
 * @details
 * The RPS detects very-forward elastically and diffractively scattered protons
 * using eight Roman Pot stations (EU, ED, WU, WD on each side of STAR), each with
 * four silicon-strip planes.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuRpsTrackPoint — a local straight-line track in one Roman Pot.  Fields:
 *     mPosition (TVector3, cm), mRpId, mClusterId[4] (per-plane cluster ids),
 *     mQuality (rpsNormal/rpsGolden/rpsNotSet), mTime[2] (ns, per PMT).
 *     Accessors: x(), y(), z(), positionVec(), rpId(), clusterId(plane), quality(),
 *     time(pmtId), planesUsed().
 *   - StMuRpsTrack — global track spanning two stations in one branch.  Fields:
 *     mTrackPoints[2] (TRef to StMuRpsTrackPoint), mP (TVector3, GeV/c),
 *     mBranch (EU=0, ED=1, WU=2, WD=3), mType (rpsLocal/rpsGlobal/rpsUndefined).
 *     Kinematic accessors: theta(), thetaRp(), phi(), phiRp(), t(beamMomentum),
 *     xi(beamMomentum), p(), pt(), eta(), time().
 *   - StMuRpsCollection — top-level container.  Stores per-RP ADC/TAC/status (8
 *     pots), per-plane geometry (offset, z, angle, orientation, status, 4 per pot),
 *     per-cluster position/energy/quality data, and vectors of StMuRpsTrackPoint*
 *     and StMuRpsTrack*.  Conversion from StRpsCollection is done in the collection
 *     constructor; no separate Util class exists.
 *
 * **MuDST storage:** Roman Pot data is embedded within a single StMuRpsCollection
 * object stored as a branch in the MuDST (accessed via StMuDst::RpsCollection()).
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTRHICf RHICf
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the RHICf very-forward calorimeter.
 * @details
 * RHICf is a small calorimeter placed at the STAR zero-degree location to measure
 * very-forward (η > 6) neutral particles (photons, neutrons, π⁰).  It consists of
 * two GSO-crystal towers (2 × 2 cm² small arm, 4 × 4 cm² large arm), each with
 * 16 scintillator plates and a GSO-bar position-sensitive layer.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuRHICfRawHit — raw ADC data for one event.  Stores RHICf-internal run and
 *     event numbers (distinct from STAR numbers), runType, bunchNumber, trigger,
 *     run timestamps, TRGM word, and ADC arrays: mPlateADC[tower][plate][range]
 *     (and mPlateADCDelay for pedestal), mGSOSmallADC/mGSOLargeADC[layer][xy][bar],
 *     plus TDC, CAD0, GPI0, GPI1 words.
 *   - StMuRHICfHit — reconstructed shower information.  Provides plate energies
 *     (getPlateEnergy(tower, plate)), GSO bar energies (getGSOBarEnergy(tower,
 *     layer, xy, bar)), longitudinal shower depth at 20%/90% (getL20/getL90),
 *     number of points per tower (getPointNum), and single/multi-hit position and
 *     peak-fit arrays.  Optional analysis arrays are allocated on demand;
 *     isSaveDataArray() indicates their presence.
 *   - StMuRHICfPoint — one reconstructed particle position.  Fields: mTowerIdx
 *     (0 = small, 1 = large), mParticleID, mPointPos[2] (x/y, cm), mPointEnergy[2]
 *     (GeV), mTowerSumEnergy[2] (GeV, all / partial).
 *   - StMuRHICfCollection — holds TClonesArrays for raw hit (single entry), hit
 *     (single entry), and points.  Accessors: getRawHit(), getHit(),
 *     getPoint(index), numberOfPoints().
 *   - StMuRHICfUtil — converts StRHICfCollection ↔ StMuRHICfCollection via
 *     fillMuRHICf() / fillRHICf().
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** RHICfRawHit, RHICfHit, RHICfPoint
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTFTT sTGC Forward Tracker (FTT)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR sTGC Forward Tracker.
 * @details
 * The FTT tracks charged particles at forward rapidity (1 < η < 4) using four planes
 * of small-strip Thin Gap Chambers (sTGCs), each plane divided into four quadrants.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuFttRawHit — one VMM chip channel readout.  Hardware address: sector,
 *     RDO (Readout Data Object), FEB (Front-End Board), VMM chip, channel.  Raw
 *     data: ADC amplitude, BCID, time-bin (TB), BCID delta.  Mapped geometry:
 *     plane, quadrant, row, strip, orientation.  MC: idTruth, qaTruth.
 *   - StMuFttCluster — a 1-D strip cluster on one plane.  Fields: id, plane,
 *     quadrant, orientation, nStrips, sumAdc (0th moment), x (1st moment, local
 *     grid), sigma (2nd moment).  TRefArrays: mRawHits, mNeighbors, mPoints.
 *     MC: idTruth.
 *   - StMuFttPoint — intersection of two orthogonal clusters giving a 2-D position.
 *     Fields: plane, quadrant, x/y (local cm), mXYZ (TVector3, global STAR coords),
 *     mClusters (TRefArray of parent clusters).  MC: idTruth, qaTruth.
 *   - StMuFttCollection — holds TClonesArrays for raw hits, clusters, and points.
 *   - StMuFttUtil — converts StFttCollection ↔ StMuFttCollection.  Rebuilds
 *     hit↔cluster↔point cross-references after filling via rebuildRelationships().
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** FttRawHit, FttCluster, FttPoint
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTFST Forward Silicon Tracker (FST)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for the STAR Forward Silicon Tracker.
 * @details
 * The FST provides silicon tracking at 1 < η < 4 using three detector discs.
 * Each disc has 12 wedges × 3 sensors per wedge read out by APV25 chips.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuFstRawHit — one APV channel with per-timebin ADC values.  Fields:
 *     channelId and geoId [0,36863], seedhitflag, mCharge[kFstNumTimeBins] and
 *     mChargeErr[kFstNumTimeBins] (pedestal/CMN-subtracted in physics mode),
 *     mMaxTimeBin, mIdTruth.  Geometry decoded from geoId: getDisk() [1–3],
 *     getWedge() [1–36], getPhiStrip() [0–127], getRStrip() [0–7], getRdo(),
 *     getArm(), getApv(), getSensor(), getChannel().
 *   - StMuFstHit — one reconstructed cluster hit.  Fields: id, idTruth,
 *     mHardwarePosition (encodes disk/wedge/sensor), apv, maxTimeBin, meanRStrip,
 *     meanPhiStrip, charge, chargeErr, nRawHits/nRawHitsR/nRawHitsPhi, localPosition
 *     [3], mXYZ (TVector3, global STAR coords).  Geometry: getDisk() [1–3],
 *     getWedge() [1–36], getSensor() [0–2].
 *   - StMuFstCollection — holds TClonesArrays for raw hits and hits.
 *   - StMuFstUtil — converts StFstHitCollection + StFstEvtCollection →
 *     StMuFstCollection via fillMuFst(), and back via fillFst().
 *
 * **MuDST branches:** FstRawHit, FstHit
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTFWD Forward Tracks (FWD)
 * @ingroup StMuDSTDetectors
 * @brief MuDST classes for STAR forward reconstructed tracks.
 * @details
 * Forward tracks are reconstructed using the GenFit framework, combining hits from
 * FST, FTT, and FCS to cover 1 < η < 4.
 *
 * **Classes:**
 *   - StMuFwdTrackProjection — track state at one detector plane.  Fields: mDetId
 *     (UChar_t), mXYZ (TVector3, position), mMom (TVector3, momentum), mCov[9]
 *     (Float_t, 3×3 position covariance).  Methods: dx(), dy(), dz() = √(diag cov).
 *   - StMuFwdTrackSeedPoint — seed-step hit used in track finding.  Fields: mXYZ
 *     (TVector3), mSector (Short_t), mTrackId (UShort_t), mCov[9].
 *   - StMuFwdTrack — one reconstructed forward track.  Quality: mDidFitConverge,
 *     mDidFitConvergeFully, mNumberOfFailedPoints, mNumberOfSeedPoints,
 *     mNumberOfFitPoints, mChi2, mNDF, mPval.  Kinematics: mPrimaryMomentum
 *     (TVector3, GeV/c), mCharge.  Detector information: mProjections (std::vector
 *     of StMuFwdTrackProjection, one per plane), mFTTPoints and mFSTPoints
 *     (std::vector of StMuFwdTrackSeedPoint), mEcalClusters and mHcalClusters
 *     (TRefArray to matched StMuFcsCluster objects).  Track origin: mDCA[3] (cm),
 *     mVtxIndex (UCHAR_MAX = global).  MC truth: mIdTruth, mQATruth.
 *     isPrimary() returns true when mVtxIndex != UCHAR_MAX.
 *   - StMuFwdTrackCollection — TClonesArray of StMuFwdTrack.
 *   - StMuFwdTrackUtil — converts StFwdTrackCollection ↔ StMuFwdTrackCollection.
 *     fillMuFwdTrack() takes an StMuFcsUtil* to resolve FCS cluster references.
 *
 * **MuDST branch:** FwdTrack
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
